---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const entry = {
  "id": "harvard_ii1_12",
  "series": "Band II 1 (1663 - 1685)",
  "seq": 12,
  "text": "<p> [[39.1]] <b>12. JAKOB THOMASIUS AN LEIBNIZ</p>\n<p> [[39.2]] Leipzig, 6. (16.) Mai 1669. [11.13.]</b></p>\n<p> [[39.12]] Ignosce quaeso, si literis prolixis nihil minus, quam prolixas reddidero; non quod\n[[39.13]] gratiam illis prolixitas abstulerit (addidit potius), sed quod otium exiguum, ac nundinarum\n[[39.14]] strepitus non sinat de prolixitate cogitare, quam ipse quoque mihi ultro remittis. Commodum\n[[39.15]] autem sic cecidit, ut ad disputationem illam tuam honeste silere possim, cui quemadmodum\n[[39.16]] satisfacerem, non reperirem. Quanquam enim, quae disseris, legenti mihi non plane excusserunt\n[[39.17]] opinionem pristinam, labefactare tamen sunt visa, et parare me non mediocriter, vel ad abjiciendam\n[[39.18]] sententiam, vel forte ad conciliandam cum tua aliquo modo. Sed verum ut fatear,\n[[39.19]] nescio, si rationes computo meas, sitne consultum mihi, hoc in campo tecum congredi, in quo\n[[39.20]] non sum ita ego versatus, ut paria tecum audeam facere, praesertim cum res ipsa non mediocrem\n[[39.21]] requirat artium mathematicarum peritiam, in quibus desipiam, si tecum congrediar.\n[[39.22]] Adde, quo longe tu me es felicior, cujus vernantissima aetas in ea incidit tempora, in quibus\n[[39.23]] prope debellatum foret: mea contra juventus omnis consumta est in illis aevi barbari reliquiis, e\n[[39.24]] quibus utcunque paullatim emersisse satis habui ad qualemcunque eruditionis profectum. Quare\n[[39.25]] feres aequo animo, si tecum ita jam paciscar, ut si maxime nihil umquam eruditissimae\n[[39.26]] disquisitioni respondero, feram impune sane; cum in proelium me voces plane insuetum mihi,\n[[39.27]] liceat, quod cautorum est militum, intra vallum me continere. Si tamen erit otium cogitandi,\n[[39.28]] rescribam aliquid fortasse aliquando. </p>\n<p> [[39.29]] De illustrissimo Boineburgio non reperio, quin gratias agam tibi, qui tanti herois non\n[[39.30]] favorem mihi modo, sed amorem plane singularem conciliaveris. Quid enim quaeris? Scioppium\n[[39.31]] suum donavit mihi ultro, cum alterius exempli copiam speret. Caetera prae pudore taceo.\n[[40.1]] Te rogo, perficias apud eum, ut et in benevolentia perseveret (quamquam virtus ejus dubitare\n[[40.2]] me non sinit), et in me laudando sit parcior. Quae nova mihi non pauca nuncias, gratissima\n[[40.3]] fuerunt: Magis me tibi devincies, si per te cognovero, quemadmodum illa tua <i>confessio naturae\n[[40.4]] contra Atheistas</i>, quam Cl. Spizelius edidit, emendanda sit. </p>\n<p> [[40.5]] De Sarcmasio quid alii sentiant, ipsi viderint. Apud nos quidem neminem scio, cui se\n[[40.6]] insania hominis cum flagitiosa rabie conjuncta probet. Nec dubitare possumus, quin illi viri,\n[[40.7]] quibus blanditur, malint eum de se siluisse in libello famoso. Nec enim unquam ipsi per\n[[40.8]] calcatas aliorum ruinas emergere pulchrum putaverunt. Sed tanta hominem agit vesania, nescio\n[[40.9]] dicam an malitia, ut adscito jam Xavierii Parani nomine, vindicias adversus Lentulum, Nasturtium,\n[[40.10]] Burgoldensem emiserit. Imprimi haec talia nemine vetante, non possum satis mirari.\n[[40.11]] Nec spero futurum esse, ut ad se homo redeat, nisi majori vi coërceatur. </p>\n<p> [[40.12]] Haberes cum his literis meam de origine animae humanae disputationem, nisi monuisset\n[[40.13]] Freislebius, commodius a mercatoribus, si quid tale vellem, quam per postam fieri posse. Ipse\n[[40.14]] interim et ejus curandae negotium suscepit. In ea, cum poscente argumento disputanda quaedam\n[[40.15]] mihi fuerint adversus Pontificios doctores, nescio num et Illustrissimo Boineburgio mittendum\n[[40.16]] sit exemplum, ne forte incivilitati imputet, si ea mittam, in quibus aliter de argumento\n[[40.17]] gravissimo a me disputatur, quam ipse vellet. Promisi interim ad futuras nundinas disputationes\n[[40.18]] quasi sex, <greek>sỳn ue^ṽ eĭpeĩn</greek>, quas jam diu affectas <i>de stoica mundi exustione</i> habeo. Tu optimum\n[[40.19]] Maecenatem meo nomine humillime salutabis, proque egregio munere gratias una mecum ages.\n[[40.20]] Vale, et aridae scriptioni ignosce. Lips. d. 6 Maii, 1669. </p>\n<p> [[40.21]] De studiorum meorum ratione nondum potui fuse ad Illustrissimum Boineburgium disserere,\n[[40.22]] angustia temporis praeclusus. Faciam id alias. </p>\n",
  "number": "12.",
  "title": "JAKOB THOMASIUS AN LEIBNIZ",
  "date": "Leipzig, 6. (16.) Mai 1669. [11.13.]"
};
---

<Layout title={`${entry.title || entry.id} - Leibniz Writings`}>
  <article data-pagefind-body>
    <header class="entry-header">
      <h1 data-pagefind-meta="title">{entry.title || entry.id}</h1>

      <div class="entry-meta">
        {entry.date && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Date:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="date">{entry.date}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Series:</strong>
          <span data-pagefind-meta="series">{entry.series}</span>
        </div>

        {entry.number && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Number:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="number">{entry.number}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Sequence:</strong>
          <span>{entry.seq}</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- View Toggle -->
    <div class="view-controls">
      <button id="translation-view-btn" class="view-btn active">Translation View</button>
      <button id="scholarly-view-btn" class="view-btn">Scholarly View</button>
    </div>

    <div class="entry-content" data-pagefind-meta="excerpt:12. JAKOB THOMASIUS AN LEIBNIZ Leipzig, 6. (16.) Mai 1669. [11.13.] Ignosce quaeso, si literis prolixis nihil minus, quam prolixas reddidero; non quod gratiam illis prolixitas abstulerit (addidit potius), sed quod otium exiguum, ac nundinarum strepitus non sinat de prolixitate cogitare, quam ipse qu...">

      <!-- Translation-friendly continuous text -->
      <div id="translation-view" class="text-view active">
        <div class="translation-notice">
          <p><strong>📖 Translation View:</strong> Continuous text optimized for browser translation tools.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="continuous-text" translate="yes" lang="unknown" id="continuous-text">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
        <div class="line-numbers-reference" id="line-numbers-ref">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Detailed scholarly view with line numbers -->
      <div id="scholarly-view" class="text-view">
        <div class="scholarly-notice">
          <p><strong>📚 Scholarly View:</strong> Original text with line number annotations preserved.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="annotated-text" id="annotated-text">
          {entry.text.split('\n').map(paragraph =>
            paragraph.trim() && <p set:html={paragraph} />
          )}
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </article>

  <nav class="entry-navigation">
    <a href="/" class="back-link">← Back to Search</a>
  </nav>
</Layout>

<style>
  .entry-header {
    margin-bottom: 30px;
    padding-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border);
  }

  .entry-header h1 {
    color: var(--primary);
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .entry-meta {
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .meta-item {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .meta-item strong {
    color: var(--text);
    min-width: 80px;
  }

  .meta-item span {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    flex: 1;
  }

  .entry-content {
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .text-content {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 30px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .text-content :global(p) {
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .text-content :global(p:last-child) {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .text-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .entry-navigation {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: 20px;
  }

  .back-link {
    color: var(--primary);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 500;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    color: var(--primary-dark);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  /* View Toggle Controls */
  .view-controls {
    display: flex;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-bottom: 20px;
  }

  .view-btn {
    background: transparent;
    border: 2px solid var(--border);
    padding: 8px 16px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    cursor: pointer;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    transition: all 0.2s;
  }

  .view-btn:hover {
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .view-btn.active {
    background: var(--primary);
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: white;
  }

  /* Text Views */
  .text-view {
    display: none;
  }

  .text-view.active {
    display: block;
  }

  /* Translation View */
  .translation-notice, .scholarly-notice {
    background: var(--background);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    font-size: 14px;
  }

  .continuous-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 2px solid var(--primary);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 25px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    font-size: 16px;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 15px;
  }

  .line-numbers-reference {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 13px;
    padding: 10px;
    background: var(--background);
    border-radius: 4px;
  }

  /* Scholarly View */
  .annotated-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 20px;
  }

  .text-line {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .line-refs {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 4px;
    min-width: 80px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .line-num {
    background: var(--primary);
    color: white;
    padding: 2px 6px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-family: monospace;
  }

  .line-content {
    flex: 1;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .line-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .line-content :global(i) {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .entry-meta {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .view-controls {
      flex-direction: column;
    }

    .text-line {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 6px;
    }

    .line-refs {
      min-width: auto;
    }
  }
</style>

<script>
  // Process text for translation view
  function processTextForTranslation(text) {
    if (!text) return { translationText: '', lineNumbers: [] };

    const lines = text.split('\n');
    let translationText = '';
    const lineNumbers = [];

    lines.forEach(line => {
      const trimmedLine = line.trim();
      if (!trimmedLine) return;

      // Extract line numbers
      const lineNumberMatch = trimmedLine.match(/\[\[(\d+\.\d+)\]\]/g);
      const extractedNumbers = lineNumberMatch ?
        lineNumberMatch.map(m => m.replace(/\[|\]/g, '')) : [];

      // Remove line number markers and HTML tags for continuous text
      let contentOnly = trimmedLine
        .replace(/\[\[\d+\.\d+\]\]/g, '')
        .replace(/<\/?[^>]+(>|$)/g, '')
        .replace(/\s+/g, ' ')
        .trim();

      if (contentOnly) {
        if (translationText) translationText += ' ';
        translationText += contentOnly;
        lineNumbers.push(...extractedNumbers);
      }
    });

    return {
      translationText: translationText.trim(),
      lineNumbers: lineNumbers
    };
  }

  // View switching and text processing
  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
    const translationBtn = document.getElementById('translation-view-btn');
    const scholarlyBtn = document.getElementById('scholarly-view-btn');
    const translationView = document.getElementById('translation-view');
    const scholarlyView = document.getElementById('scholarly-view');
    const continuousTextDiv = document.getElementById('continuous-text');
    const lineNumbersRef = document.getElementById('line-numbers-ref');

    // Process the text for translation view
    if (continuousTextDiv && lineNumbersRef && entry && entry.text) {
      const processed = processTextForTranslation(entry.text);
      continuousTextDiv.textContent = processed.translationText;

      if (processed.lineNumbers.length > 0) {
        lineNumbersRef.innerHTML = `<small><strong>Line numbers:</strong> ${processed.lineNumbers.join(', ')}</small>`;
      }
    }

    // View switching functionality
    if (translationBtn && scholarlyBtn && translationView && scholarlyView) {
      translationBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        translationBtn.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyBtn.classList.remove('active');
        translationView.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.remove('active');
      });

      scholarlyBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        scholarlyBtn.classList.add('active');
        translationBtn.classList.remove('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.add('active');
        translationView.classList.remove('active');
      });
    }
  });
</script>